From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.local>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add OpenSCAD str() and chr() expression support

This patch is prepared for future use and is not applied.

Scope:
- add string values to ExpressionSyntax::Value;
- parse string literals in validate/evaluate paths;
- add ExpressionSyntax::evaluateString();
- implement str(...) and chr(...);
- make len("abc") return 3;
- preserve numeric evaluate() behavior by collapsing strings to 0.

Notes:
- This is expression-layer support only. Parser call sites such as text(...)
  still need to call evaluateString() explicitly if they want text(str(...)).
- OpenSCAD chr() accepts one or more Unicode code points and returns a string.

